# S4-EtPBC-A, R4-T2 (A3g): flat descent of vanishing tensors to finitely generated subalgebras

For a flat `A`-algebra `S` (in use: `S = Â`, flat by `AdicCompletion.flat_of_isNoetherian`) and an `A`-module `B`:

* **`exists_fg_lift`**: finitely many elements of `S ⊗[A] B` all come from `C₀ ⊗[A] B` for one f.g. `C₀ ≤ S`.
* **`desc_one`** / **`desc_fg`**: finitely many elements of `C₀ ⊗[A] B` whose images in `S ⊗[A] B` vanish already
  vanish in `C ⊗[A] B` for a f.g. `C` with `C₀ ≤ C` (equational criterion for vanishing + flatness of `S`).
* **`rTensor_inclusion_mono`**: such a vanishing persists along any larger subalgebra.
* **`tmap_id_apply`**, **`desc_mvPoly`**: the same for finitely many polynomials over `C₀ ⊗[A] B` (`B` an algebra),
  coefficientwise, with the ring maps `Algebra.TensorProduct.map (inclusion h) (AlgHom.id A B)`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

namespace RamanujanPetersson.EtPBC.Cov

open TensorProduct

universe u

section Mod

end Mod

section Alg

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : Type u} [CommRing S] [Algebra A S]
  {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

theorem tmap_id_apply {D D' : Type u} [CommRing D] [CommRing D'] [Algebra A D] [Algebra A D']
    (f : D →ₐ[A] D') (x : D ⊗[A] B) :
    Algebra.TensorProduct.map f (AlgHom.id A B) x = f.toLinearMap.rTensor B x := by
  induction x using TensorProduct.induction_on with
  | zero => simp only [map_zero]
  | tmul a b =>
    first
      | (simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, LinearMap.rTensor_tmul]; done)
      | rfl
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy]

end Alg

end RamanujanPetersson.EtPBC.Cov

end

end

-- ===== S4.Def_RP_EtPBC_A_CovAs5a =====
section

/-!
# S4-EtPBC-A, R4-T2 (A3 assembly, As5a): lifting polynomials and memberships to a f.g. subalgebra

For a flat `A`-algebra `S` and an `A`-algebra `B`, with `tvC B C : C ⊗ B → S ⊗ B` and, for `C ≤ D`,
`tiC B h : C ⊗ B → D ⊗ B`:
* `exists_lift_polys`: finitely many polynomials over `S ⊗ B` come from one f.g. `C`;
* `exists_lift_monic`: a monic polynomial over `S ⊗ B` comes from a monic one over `C ⊗ B`;
* **`desc_mem`**: finitely many ideal memberships `x_k ∈ (g)` over `S ⊗ B` already hold over `C ⊗ B` for a f.g.
  `C ≥ C₀` (cofactors lifted by `exists_lift_polys`, the identities descended by `desc_mvPoly`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

namespace RamanujanPetersson.EtPBC.Cov

open TensorProduct

universe u

section Lift

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : Type u} [CommRing S] [Algebra A S]

/-- `C ⊗ B → S ⊗ B`. -/
abbrev tvC (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] (C : Subalgebra A S) : C ⊗[A] B →+* S ⊗[A] B :=
  (Algebra.TensorProduct.map C.val (AlgHom.id A B)).toRingHom

end Lift

end RamanujanPetersson.EtPBC.Cov

end

